id: quiz.k8s.probes
kind: quiz
track: kubernetes
title: Readiness, liveness, startup
question: Explain the three probes and give a case where each one is the right tool.
expects:
  - readiness
  - liveness
  - startup
  - endpoint list
  - restart
misuse:
  - liveness checking a dependency => a slow database restarts every replica
  - readiness that never fails => broken pods keep receiving traffic
related:
  - k8s.probe.readiness
  - k8s.probe.liveness
  - k8s.probe.startup
  - design.health-checking
follow_ups:
  - what does a failing readiness probe do to the Service?
answer: |
  Readiness gates traffic: failing removes the pod from the endpoint list without
  a restart (use it when the app cannot serve right now). Liveness restarts the
  container: use it only for a wedged process, never for a slow dependency.
  Startup gives a slow boot a budget and suspends the other two until it passes.
